# PyRate-skills — ignore rules
#
# Two groups only: (1) Python/OS/editor junk this workspace generates, and
# (2) the files a PyRate run actually writes into the working directory. Every
# name in group 2 is copied from a form the mirrored documentation prints, and
# each line cites the mirror that prints it (line numbers include the mirror
# frontmatter). Nothing is guessed: if the corpus does not print the name, the
# name is not here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1) tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.DS_Store

# virtual environments. `pyrate_env` is the name the venv tutorial prints
# ("python -m venv desired_path_to_env/pyrate_env",
#  pyrate-installation/references/virtual-environment.md:19)
.venv/
venv/
env/
pyrate_env/

# ---------------------------------------- 2) inputs generated by extract.ages
# "The previous step generated two files: a text file (*_SpeciesList.txt) ...
#  and a python file (*_PyRate.py)" (pyrate-input-file/references/tutorial-1.md:40)
*_PyRate.py
*_SpeciesList.txt

# ------------------------------------------------- 2) run output log/summary
# "A typical PyRate analysis produces three output files" — *_sum.txt,
# *_mcmc.log, *_marginal_rates.log, plus *_marginal_likelihood.txt for -A 1
# (pyrate-summarize-results/references/summarize-results.md:12-30)
*_sum.txt
*_mcmc.log
*_marginal_rates.log
*_marginal_likelihood.txt

# RJMCMC (-A 4) writes *_sp_rates.log and *_ex_rates.log instead
# (pyrate-rjmcmc/references/tutorial-3.md:56-57)
*_sp_rates.log
*_ex_rates.log

# the log folder: "saved in a folder named pyrate_mcmc_logs in the same
# directory as the input file" (pyrate-input-file/references/tutorial-1.md:194)
pyrate_mcmc_logs/

# ------------------------------------------------- 2) R plotting output
# "Two output files are generated: an R script named '*_RTTplot.r' and a pdf
# file named '*_RTTplot.pdf'" (pyrate-summarize-results/references/summarize-results.md:40)
*_RTTplot.r
*_RTTplot.pdf

# ------------------------------- 2) times tables written by -ginput / -tag
# names of the form Canidae_1_G_se_est.txt / Carnivora_occs_1_Grj_se_est.txt
# (pyrate-continuous-covariates/references/tutorial-2.md:31-33,
#  pyrate-bdnn/references/tutorial-bdnn.md:482)
*_se_est.txt
# the combined table the docs print as "...se_ext.txt"
# (pyrate-continuous-covariates/references/tutorial-2.md:45-49)
*se_ext.txt

# -------------------------------------------------------- 2) BDNN output
# "The -BDNN_pred_importance command creates seven files in the log files'
# folder": _coefficient_of_rate_variation.csv, _sp/_ex_predictor_influence.csv
# (pyrate-bdnn/references/tutorial-bdnn.md:96-106) and *_pdp.csv
# (pyrate-bdnn/references/tutorial-bdnn.md:320)
*_coefficient_of_rate_variation.csv
*_sp_predictor_influence.csv
*_ex_predictor_influence.csv
*_pdp.csv
# "-combBDNN ... generates five output files named combined_[n]_mcmc.log,
# combined_[n]_per_species_rates.log, combined_[n]_sp_rates.log,
# combined_[n]_ex_rates.log, and combined_[n].pkl"
# (pyrate-bdnn/references/tutorial-bdnn.md:457)
combined_*_mcmc.log
combined_*_per_species_rates.log
combined_*_sp_rates.log
combined_*_ex_rates.log
combined_*.pkl
